Z||000002||Oreif||11-30-2001||01:54 AM||||AAHHH not Millington!! (J/K)<BR>I was stationed there in 1982.<BR>It's probably changed a whole lot since I was there. We use to go to a bar in Memphis called "Silky Sullivan's" That had a drink there that came in a gallon paint can. It was called "The Diver" for more than one reason.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Not too bad of a place. The actual Air Station was on the north and the training was on the south side. I heard the school's got moved.<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||11-30-2001||08:32 AM||||Sounds like fun. Atleast maybe now you'll have time to work on the Fieros.lol<P>Take care,<BR>Jeff||||reg||1
Z||000004||WampusCat||11-30-2001||09:55 AM||||Hey Oreif,  I was in Avionics school in Millington in '84.  I live a block from where the old Silky's used to be.  They just knocked the building down a few months ago to make parking space.  The new Silky's is on Beale street now.  They have a pen with goats by the patio which is cool, but no tree in the middle of the dance floor to slam dance with like the old place.  "The Diver, guaranteed to make you go down!"  Prince Mongo has a Castle-looking house for a bar in a wealthy neighborhood now.  He hauled in a bunch of sand to make a beach in his front yard.  He's in court all the time with his neighbors.  I spent 13.5 years in the Marines and the Millington chow hall was the worst by far.||||reg||1
Z||000005||2birds||11-30-2001||10:11 PM||||Since I've been to pretty much every other Navy installation  over the past 16 years, ('cept for San Diego), I'm looking forward to it.  I'm gonna be a detailer.  I'll see more of the world doing that than I have in the past 5 years on a boomer.<P>The Air Station part is closed, now it's just a support activity for the region, with the personnel and recruiting headquarters there.  <P>The best part is its proximity to home (Iowa).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||WampusCat||11-30-2001||10:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 2birds:<BR><B>...I'm gonna be a detailer...  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Cool, you can probably get some good bribery loot on that tour.  A bottle of good booze always seemed to help with assignments and orders.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||My7Fieros||12-01-2001||12:54 AM||||Kewl beans! I'll see ya then!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My7logo_1.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000008||Oreif||12-01-2001||01:25 AM||||Personnel HQ is there? Hey maybe you could locate the $385.00 they haven't paid me when I was in the Reserves back in 1986.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>You also won't be far from NIFE events too!<BR>Maybe we'll be able to see you and My7Fiero's<BR>at some events.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||maryjane||12-01-2001||12:54 PM||||WampusCat, I remember Prince Mongo's. Strange place back when I lived there.<BR>My7: They still have those places out on the Tipton County line? I think one was the Tipton Inn. I saw more brawls and fights in that place than any other bar I ever visited.<BR>That was way back when tho. Beal Street was pretty seedy; off limits to military personell. I used to walk Shore Patrol duty down there, should have gotten combat pay.<BR>And if you run across some floozie named Kitten at the club there, DON'T mention my name. <p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 12-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||TN Fieros||12-01-2001||02:37 PM||||Any of you Memphis guys going to meet up with us at the Fiero Factory next Saturday? It would be nice to finally get to meet you. And if anyone wants to make a full day of it, Ed and a lot of the guys from the Fiero Factory are going to convoy back to Nashville with us that afternoon. They are planning on visiting the Opryland Hotel and Opry Mills. It's a full day of Fiero fun! <P>We'll be leaving Nashville about 8:30 with plans to be at the Fiero Factory by around 10am. Hope to see some new faces there.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TNFiero[1].gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
